-- Demonstration accounts and sample registrations.
--
-- SEPARATED FROM THE REFERENCE DATA ON PURPOSE. Flyway runs in every environment, so anything in
-- this file reaches Production unless something stops it. These rows are development and
-- demonstration fixtures - the local login smoke test signs in as superadmin@ipie.gov.in, and the
-- role demo users exist to exercise the permission model - and they have no business in a live
-- environment holding real registrations.
--
-- Kept as a migration for now because that is the behaviour the stack has today, and changing it is
-- a separate decision. Before the first deployment to a shared environment, move this file to a
-- development-only Flyway location (spring.flyway.locations under the dev profile) so that the
-- schema is created everywhere and these rows are created only where they belong.
--
-- The rows are captured from the reference development database in current-schema form, rather than
-- carried over from the migrations that first wrote them: those were written against columns that
-- later migrations replaced, and would no longer apply. Lookup references are resolved by business
-- code because reference-data ids are generated per environment.

